\caption(Exact residual means produce the first softmax update; accuracy then hides continued changes in confidence.)
\alttext(The first panel shows class probabilities at all four input values after one round and the prior reference at one half. The second plots log loss from round zero through twenty. Tables expose the input, all eight class residual updates and selected evaluation stages.)

>> Six rows and three classes: compute targets simultaneously

Take x=(0,1,2,3,4,5) with labels (a,a,b,b,c,c). Priors are one third. Every row's
true-class residual is 2/3 and its other two residuals are −1/3. Class a can be isolated
by the first stump and class c by the last. For class \(b\), two symmetric stump splits tie;
the implementation keeps the first ascending threshold, 1.5. Its left prediction is
−1/3 and its right prediction is (2/3+2/3−1/3−1/3)/4=1/6.

At \(x=2\) after one \(\eta=.5\) step, score increments are \((-1/6,1/12,-1/6)\). Their softmax is
approximately (.304504,.390991,.304504). The class-b residual used in that same round
is still 2/3, computed before any score update. Separate class trees need not sum to
zero at each x; softmax handles the common-score offset automatically.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gbm_multiclass.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame d;
  d.add_column("x", std::vector<double>{0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5});
  d.add_column("label", std::vector<std::string>{"a", "a", "b", "b", "c", "c"});
  const dm::stats::GBMClassifier       m(d, "label ~ x", {20, .5, 1});
  const std::vector<dm::graphics::RGB> colors = {{37, 99, 235}, {220, 38, 38}, {22, 163, 74}};
  auto left = dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), right = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  for (std::size_t k = 0; k < 3; ++k) {
    std::vector<double> early, late;
    const auto          first = m.predict_detail(d, 1), last = m.predict_detail(d);
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < d.nrows(); ++i) {
      early.push_back(first.probability[i][k]);
      late.push_back(last.probability[i][k]);
    }
    left.line({0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5}, early, m.classes()[k], colors[k])
        .points({0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5}, early, "", colors[k], 4);
    right.line({0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5}, late, m.classes()[k], colors[k])
        .points({0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5}, late, "", colors[k], 4);
  }
  left.title("One round: shared starting probabilities")
      .x_label("x")
      .y_label("class probability")
      .y_limits(0, 1.5);
  right.title("Twenty rounds: confidence changes")
      .x_label("x")
      .y_label("class probability")
      .y_limits(0, 1.5);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(left).add(right).size(1100, 490).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/gbm_multiclass.svg");
  std::print(
      "Representative first-round rows (original rows 0, 2, 4):\n\n{}\n\nStage metrics:\n\n{}\n",
      m.training_step(1)
          .take_rows({0, 1, 2, 6, 7, 8, 12, 13, 14})
          .select(
              {"original_row",
               "class",
               "before_probability",
               "pseudo_residual",
               "tree_value",
               "after_probability"})
          .to_md(8),
      m.staged_evaluation(d)
          .take_rows({0, 1, 20})
          .select({"round", "accuracy", "mean_log_loss", "brier"})
          .to_md(8));
}
```
